<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>East meets West on this extraordinary 16-day odyssey spanning China and Uzbekistan — the two greatest civilizations of the ancient Silk Road. Begin in Beijing, China's imperial capital, and follow the trade route westward through Xi'an, the Hexi Corridor, and the desert oases of Xinjiang. Cross into Uzbekistan to explore the turquoise domes of Samarkand, the sacred heart of Bukhara, and the timeless walled city of Khiva. This is the Silk Road as it was meant to be experienced — a grand journey connecting empires, cultures, and millennia of history.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Stand on the Great Wall at Mutianyu</li><li>Face the Terracotta Warriors in Xi'an</li>
      <li>Explore the Mogao Caves of Dunhuang</li><li>Walk the Great Wall's western end at Jiayuguan</li>
      <li>Experience Kashgar's legendary Sunday Market</li>
      <li>Marvel at Registan Square in Samarkand</li>
      <li>Wander the domed bazaars of Bukhara</li>
      <li>Discover the ancient city of Khiva — a living museum</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Beijing</h4><p>Arrive at Beijing Capital Airport. Transfer to your hotel. Evening welcome dinner featuring Peking duck, the capital's signature dish.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Beijing 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Beijing — Great Wall & Forbidden City</h4><p>Morning drive to Mutianyu Great Wall for a walk on the world's most famous fortification. Afternoon visit to the Forbidden City — the imperial palace of 24 emperors across 500 years.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Beijing 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Beijing ✈ Xi'an</h4><p>Morning flight to Xi'an, the ancient capital where the Silk Road began. Visit the Big Wild Goose Pagoda and stroll through the Muslim Quarter. Evening Tang Dynasty music and dance performance.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xi'an 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an — Terracotta Warriors</h4><p>Full morning at the Army of Terracotta Warriors — 8,000 life-sized soldiers guarding China's first emperor for over 2,200 years. Afternoon cycling on the ancient City Wall with panoramic views.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xi'an 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an → Lanzhou (High-speed train)</h4><p>High-speed train to Lanzhou (approx. 3.5 hours). Afternoon walk along the Yellow River waterfront and visit the iconic Iron Bridge. Evening sampling of Lanzhou's famous hand-pulled noodles.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Lanzhou 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lanzhou → Jiayuguan</h4><p>Drive through the Hexi Corridor to Jiayuguan (approx. 6 hours with scenic stops). Afternoon visit to the Jiayuguan Fortress — the western terminus of the Great Wall, standing at the edge of the Gobi Desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Jiayuguan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan → Dunhuang</h4><p>Morning at the Overhanging Great Wall. Drive through the Gobi to Dunhuang (5 hours). Evening free to explore the Dunhuang Night Market.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full UNESCO day. Morning at the Mogao Caves exploring a millennium of Buddhist art. Afternoon camel ride on the Singing Sand Dunes and sunset at Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang → Turpan → Urumqi</h4><p>Morning high-speed train to Turpan (4 hours). Visit the Jiaohe Ruins and Karez irrigation system. Continue to Urumqi by evening. Stroll through Erdaoqiao Grand Bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi ✈ Kashgar</h4><p>Morning flight to Kashgar. Afternoon exploration of the Old City — a living museum of Uyghur culture. Visit the Id Kah Mosque and watch the sun set from a rooftop teahouse.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market</h4><p>Experience the legendary Kashgar Sunday Market — sheep, silk, spices, and the ancient rhythms of Central Asian trade. Afternoon at Abakh Khoja Tomb. Free evening to explore the Old City.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar ✈ Tashkent</h4><p>Morning flight across the Pamirs to Tashkent, Uzbekistan's modern capital. Afternoon city tour: Khast Imam Complex (home of the ancient Quran of Caliph Uthman), Chorsu Bazaar, and Independence Square.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent → Samarkand (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning Afrosiyob high-speed train to Samarkand (2 hours). Afternoon at Registan Square — three magnificent madrasahs with turquoise domes. Visit the Gur-e-Amir Mausoleum, resting place of Tamerlane. Evening light show at Registan.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Samarkand 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand → Bukhara</h4><p>Morning at Shah-i-Zinda Necropolis and Bibi-Khanym Mosque. Afternoon train to Bukhara (1.5 hours). Evening walk around Lyab-i Hauz — the city's central pool surrounded by ancient madrasahs and teahouses.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Bukhara 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara → Khiva (via desert drive)</h4><p>Morning at the Ark Fortress, Kalon Minaret, and the domed trading bazaars. Drive through the Kyzylkum Desert to Khiva (6-7 hours), the most remote of Uzbekistan's Silk Road cities. Arrive in this open-air museum frozen in time.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Khiva 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>16</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva — Itchan Kala & Depart</h4><p>Morning exploration of Itchan Kala — the perfectly preserved inner walled city, a UNESCO World Heritage site. Walk the city walls for panoramic views. Transfer to Urgench Airport for departure. Your epic Silk Road journey concludes.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>15 nights 4-star hotel accommodation (twin-share)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>English-speaking guide throughout (China & Uzbekistan)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All domestic/international flights & high-speed trains</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Private air-conditioned vehicle & driver</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Meals as indicated (B=Breakfast, L=Lunch, D=Dinner)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All entrance fees & listed activities</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Airport transfers on arrival & departure</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Uzbekistan visa support letter</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>What's Excluded</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>International flights to Beijing / from Urgench</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>China & Uzbekistan visa fees</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Personal expenses & tips</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Single room supplement ($680)</p></div>
    </div>

    </div>

